'stem-chateau-berliquet|2016':{blend:{ME:75,CF:25},yld:48,months:'12-16',oak:50,src:'Berliquet-2016-FT-FR-555.pdf',via:'trade',pick:{ALL:'10-18|'}},
'stem-chateau-berliquet|2022':{blend:{ME:65,CF:35},alc:14.5,ph:3.55,yld:45,months:'16',src:'FT-2022-BERLIQUET-FR.pdf',via:'trade',oak:44,pick:{ALL:'09-14|'}},
'stem-chateau-cote-de-baleau|2013':{blend:{CS:5,ME:80,CF:15},ph:3.65,yld:35,months:'18',src:'Cote-de-Baleau-2013.pdf',via:'trade',note:'After a cold winter with slightly above-average rainfall, January and February are particularly wet and cold. The spring too is very wet, with little sunshine and colder than the seasonal average, which brings budbreak around 10 April, rather late, a fairly uneven growth and a very strong fungal pressure, and that right up to flowering, mid-flowering falling on 17 June, producing considerable coulure. The summer finally arrived in July, with maximum temperatures above 30°C from the 6th to the 26th. That helped the vines catch up somewhat, but green harvesting and leaf-thinning were necessary.',taste:'Côte de Baleau 2013 releases a red fruit and elegant floral notes. On the palate there is a fine balance with supple, well-integrated tannins. The finish is silky and straight.',alc:13,pick:{ALL:'10-02|10-17'}},
'stem-chateau-cote-de-baleau|2023':{blend:{ME:95,CF:5},ph:3.7,yld:50,months:'14',oak:25,src:'Fiche-Technique-2023_Cote-de-Baleau_FR.pdf',via:'trade',taste:'A fine cherry colour. A nose on the fruit, fine and subtle. Supple and suave on the palate, with a very fine balance.',ttl:1,note:'Great generosity. Although 2023 can be filed as a vintage “of its time” by its early growing cycle, it is nonetheless very difficult to compare with any other vintage. With a tropical spring and a dry, moderate summer marked by two very hot spells, it has to our mind no counterpart.',ntl:1,pick:{ALL:'09-14|10-03'}},
'stem-chateau-cote-de-baleau|2024':{blend:{ME:95,CF:5},ph:3.7,yld:32,months:'14',oak:25,src:'Chateau-Cote-de-Baleau_millesime-2024.pdf',via:'trade',alc:13.5,pick:{ALL:'09-25|10-07'}},
